      "contextFingerprint": "c197be9ea795e9b23a28a41d343f4993496b9bf29dc574ad3038f519c531d792",
      "sourceText": "WSL2默认是NAT模式，也就是拿Windows当网关，WSL2是Windows的下级设备，这样的话，WSL2和Windows并不处于同一网段，WSL2只能和Windows以及Windows的上游设备进行通信，无法与和Windows同局域网的同网段设备进行通信。想要和同网段的ROS、ROS2设备进行通信，只能要么端口转发，要么设置DDS，都是非常麻烦的。",
      "translatedText": "WSL2 defaults to NAT mode, which means using Windows as the gateway, and WSL2 is a subordinate device of Windows\\. In this case, WSL2 and Windows are not on the same subnet\\. WSL2 can only communicate with Windows and the upstream devices of Windows, and cannot communicate with devices on the same subnet as Windows within the same LAN\\. To communicate with ROS and ROS2 devices on the same subnet, you can only either set up port forwarding or configure DDS, both of which are very troublesome\\.",
